#* {{quote-book|en|author=Patrick Doucette|title=Making a Fortune in Canadian Stocks: How to Get Started on the Road to Wealth with Canadian Equities|year=2000|publisher=iUniverse|isbn=978-0-595-14697-0|page=51|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=H29vko7JitMC&pg=PA51&dq=%22IPO%27ed%22&hl=&cd=2&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22IPO'ed%22&f=false|text=OnX recently '''IPO'ed''' at $7.50 per share, quickly rose to $10.50 per share and then drifted down to about $5 per share.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2012/10/gallows-humor-the-dark-jokes-of-weibo-as-chinas-stock-market-tanked/263030/|title=Gallows Humor: The Dark Jokes of Weibo as China's Stock Market Tanked|work=The Atlantic|date=2012-10-01|author=Rachel Lu|passage=@大学生讲坛 tweets, “A stock market investor asks Hades, ‘What level of hell is this?’ Hades replies, ‘The 18th.’ The investor tears up out of happiness, ‘Finally I've managed to buy at the bottom!’ Hades looks at him with a smile, ‘Don't you know that hell has '''IPOed''' and expanded to 36 levels?’”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022|author=Jimmy Soni|title=The Founders: The Story of Paypal and the Entrepreneurs Who Shaped Silicon Valley|publisher=Simon and Schuster|isbn=9781501197253|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=1RbuDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT385&dq=%22IPO%27ed%22&hl=&cd=5&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22IPO'ed%22&f=false|text=The extra scrutiny was a sign of the times, but having never '''IPO-ed''' a company before, most of the executive team took it as par for the course.}}

